abstract: 'Qi zheng lue shu (editorial translation: Brief accounts of remarkable cases) is
  a collection of case records and hospital reports compiled by John Glasgow Kerr at the Medical
  Missionary Society''s Hospital at Canton (Bodleian Sinica 1784; catalogued 1864–1868). It
  includes records and captions concerning stones, tumours, eye conditions, injuries and dental
  conditions, alongside annual reports, accounts, attendance figures, organizational business
  and publishing notices. It supports histories of medicine, medical missions, charity, patient
  narratives and medical illustration. The witness''s preface dated 1869 and appendix dated
  1873 are recorded separately. This version provides 617 text units from 60 original printed
  faces in JSON, TXT and TEI linked to source locations, with unit-level changes and small-note
  relationships. The remaining 31 shared-content faces in the 91-face witness are linked to
  the existing Sinica 2021 dataset; no complete word-for-word collation of the witnesses is
  claimed. AI-assisted initial and independent source readings were compared and revised against
  the images; the text has not undergone full human collation, and unresolved readings are
  marked.'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24147371
